hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1202","Bundar told us, Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told us, Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Haram, on the authority of His uncle Abdullah bin Saad, H, and Abdullah bin Hashim, Abdul Rahman, narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah, H, and Bahr bin Nasr narrated to us Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Wahb, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Haram bin Hakim, on the authority of his uncle Abdul Allah bin Saad said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about prayer in my house and prayer in the mosque, and he said: “You may see, how close my house is From the mosque, and because I prefer to pray in my house than to pray in the mosque, except the prescribed ones.” This is the hadith of Bundar"
